. quietly mlogit top_pref b1.treat_effect_3

. margins, dydx(treat_effect_3) post

Conditional marginal effects                             Number of obs = 3,145
Model VCE: OIM

dy/dx wrt: 2.treat_effect_3 3.treat_effect_3

1._predict: Pr(top_pref==Information___Disclosures), predict(pr outcome(1))
2._predict: Pr(top_pref==Taxes___Charges), predict(pr outcome(2))
3._predict: Pr(top_pref==Mandates___Obligations), predict(pr outcome(3))
4._predict: Pr(top_pref==Continue_voluntary_action_plan), predict(pr outcome(4))

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                  |            Delta-method
                  |      dy/dx   std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
1.treat_effect_3  |  (base outcome)
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
2.treat_effect_3  |
         _predict |
               1  |   .0100289   .0215692     0.46   0.642    -.0322461    .0523038
               2  |   .0205733   .0144494     1.42   0.155    -.0077471    .0488937
               3  |  -.0261186   .0207788    -1.26   0.209    -.0668442     .014607
               4  |  -.0044835   .0130181    -0.34   0.731    -.0299986    .0210316
------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
3.treat_effect_3  |
         _predict |
               1  |  -.0060031   .0215304    -0.28   0.780    -.0482018    .0361957
               2  |  -.0049472   .0138076    -0.36   0.720    -.0320096    .0221151
               3  |  -.0385873   .0206953    -1.86   0.062    -.0791493    .0019747
               4  |   .0495376   .0144476     3.43   0.001     .0212207    .0778544
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note: dy/dx for factor levels is the discrete change from the base level.

